<pre class=metadata>
Title: The Chart Element
Shortname: chart-element
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/HTML-Additions/chart-element/spec/
Repository: arronei/HTML-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification extends HTML with a <code>chart</code> element that draws a pie, line,
    bar, or area chart from the <code>data</code> elements inside it. Each <code>data</code> element
    is a point: its text is the point's name and its <code>value</code> attribute is the number. A
    <code>series</code> element groups points, an <code>axis</code> element names an axis, a
    <code>figcaption</code> element gives the chart a title, and a <code>legend</code> element adds
    a key. The user agent lays the chart out itself. Each <code>data</code> element's box is the
    mark it draws, such as a bar or a pie wedge, so authors style marks with CSS and handle events
    on them like any other element.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

